## 1. Product principle

- ✅ **Cloud / online first.** Firestore is the system of record for account, chats, messages, plans, packages, wallets, usage, **billing & entitlements**.
- ✅ Local VigilDB on desktop is **optional cache only** — web does not depend on it.
- ✅ **One Vigil identity** everywhere: web, desktop EXE, phone browser, embed — same Firebase Auth account.
- ✅ **Unlimited devices / sessions** for the same account (no artificial device cap in Phase 1). Usage always drains **one shared wallet**.
- ✅ **Tight continuum:** Auth ↔ Packages ↔ Payment ↔ Admin ledger ↔ Desktop activation must stay one integrated loop (not three disconnected products).
- ✅ **Never** upload private repo source trees / git objects / deep index blobs to Firestore.
- ✅ Web can store **account Library assets** (prompts, images, docs the user uploads to cloud) — not the workspace monorepo.
- ✅ Vigil serves **more than developers**: Support / DB Copilot and later PM modes share the same account shell (see `04-دعم-فني-وقواعد-البيانات.mdc`).

