### 2.3 Pricing, Free tier, Checkout (CRITICAL continuum)

**Happy path (Cursor-like, Egypt-aware)**
1. User enters **User Web** (or lands from desktop “Login / Upgrade”).
2. Chooses **Buy / Upgrade / Pricing**.
3. Sees **packages**: name, price, token/quota grant, period, highlights (Free / Pro / Partner…).
4. Selects a package → **Checkout** with **diverse payment methods**.
5. Provider confirms payment → webhook/cloud function **activates entitlement** in Firestore.
6. Account flips automatically to **paid** (or **partner** if that SKU) — badge + wallet update instantly on web **and** any logged-in desktop.
7. Admin dashboard shows the customer, package, payment row, and wallet — same Firestore truth.

**Free / trial (must)**
- ✅ **Free account** path without payment (signup trial grant + seed `free`/`trial`)
- ✅ Configurable **starter tokens** + **time window** — env + seed packages `free` / `trial`
- ✅ Clear UX when free quota ends: soft block + Upgrade CTA (`evaluateWalletGate` + `/api/chat` 402)
- ✅ Free usage still writes `usageEvents` and appears in Admin

**Paid / partner activation**
- [ ] On successful payment: `subscription.status = active`, wallet credited, `user.planTier` updated
- [ ] Partner SKUs supported (same pipeline; different entitlements / branding)
- [ ] Failed / cancelled checkout does **not** mutate tier
- [ ] Idempotent webhooks (no double-credit)

**Payment provider note (Egypt)**
- Cursor-class UX (hosted checkout, many methods, webhook activation) is the **UX bar** — not a mandate to use Stripe alone.
- Egypt is **not** a Stripe-supported business country; Stripe alone misses Meeza/local wallets/Fawry/InstaPay coverage for most Egyptian buyers.
- Vigil must ship **Egypt-first local rails** (see §2.4). Optional intl rail (Stripe/Paddle/foreign entity) only as a **second** adapter for non-EG customers.

> **عربي:** طرق الدفع المحلية في مصر

### 2.4 Egypt payment rails (product requirement — local methods)

**Goal:** On Pricing/Checkout, Egyptian users see the **important local methods**, not cards-only. Prefer covering **all major rails** via one or two licensed aggregators rather than hand-rolling each telco/bank.

#### Must-offer methods (Phase 1 target)

| Method | What the user does | Notes for Vigil |
|--------|--------------------|-----------------|
| **Cards + Meeza** | Visa / Mastercard / Amex / **Meeza** debit | 3-D Secure; hosted/embedded checkout — card data never on Vigil servers |
| **InstaPay** | Pay from bank/wallet app via **QR** or **Request-to-Pay (R2P)** | CBE Instant Payment Network; **must be API-confirmed via PSP webhook** — never “send screenshot of transfer” as the product path |
| **Mobile wallets** | Pay with wallet number / OTP confirm | At minimum: **Vodafone Cash**, **Orange Cash**, **e& money** (Etisalat), **WE Pay** |
| **Fawry (reference / kiosk)** | Get a **reference code** → pay cash at Fawry outlet / Fawry channels | Async: order stays `pending_payment` until webhook; auto-expire unpaid intents |

#### Should-offer methods (Phase 1.5 / when PSP enables)

| Method | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| **Apple Pay / Google Pay** | Quick pay where device supports; often via same aggregator |
| **BNPL / installments** | valU, Sympl, Souhoola, Halan, … — useful for higher-tier annual packages; optional for SaaS tokens |
| **Aman / Masary kiosk** | Extra cash/agent reach if aggregator exposes them |
| **Bank QR / other IPN collects** | If available on chosen PSP beyond InstaPay branding |

#### Explicitly out (as primary product paths)

- Manual InstaPay to a personal IPA + admin marks paid by hand (fraud-prone; support hell) — allow only as **Admin emergency override**, logged in audit
- Cash on delivery (not relevant for digital SaaS tokens)
- Storing raw card PAN on Vigil infra

#### Recommended integration approach (best practice for Egypt SaaS)

```text
User Checkout UI
    → Vigil Payments abstraction (method = card|instapay|wallet|fawry|…)
        → Adapter A: primary Egypt aggregator (candidate: Paymob and/or Kashier)
        → Adapter B: FawryPay if needed for best-in-class reference/cash network
        → Adapter C (optional): intl Stripe/Paddle for non-EG
    → Signed webhook / Cloud Function
        → idempotent write: payments + subscription + wallet
        → Admin ledger + user tier update
```

**Aggregator shortlist (research 2026 — confirm live methods on merchant contract):**
- **Paymob** — strong Egypt aggregator; cards, Meeza, wallets, Apple/Google Pay, BNPL; Gulf expansion; FRA/CBE payments-facilitator history. Confirm **InstaPay + Fawry** enablement on *our* MID.
- **Kashier** — Egypt-focused; **documented InstaPay API** (QR + R2P), cards, wallets, bank QR, subscriptions — strong if InstaPay is a hard must on day one.
- **FawryPay** — best native **reference-number / kiosk cash** network; also cards/wallets/instalments — add if Paymob/Kashier Fawry rail is weak or unavailable on contract.
- **Geidea / Fawaterak** — alternatives for POS+online or invoice-link lightweight flows; not first pick for full Vigil checkout unless ops prefers them.

**Product decision (default proposal until user overrides):**
1. Build a **method-agnostic Payments module** in Vigil Web (UI + Firestore `payments` + webhook handler).
2. Onboard **one primary Egypt aggregator** that can enable: cards+Meeza + wallets + InstaPay (prefer contract that lists all three).
3. Add **Fawry reference** in the same checkout (via primary if available, else second adapter).
4. Keep **intl adapter** stubbed for later — do not block Egypt launch on Stripe.

#### Checkout UX rules

- ✅ Pricing amounts for EG catalog in **EGP** (display); store `currency` on package + payment
- ✅ Checkout shows methods as clear choices: Card / InstaPay / Wallet / Fawry (sandbox radios)
- ✅ Sync methods (`card`, `wallet` instant confirm) → activate immediately (sandbox)
- 🟨 Async methods (`fawry`, InstaPay pending) → UI **في انتظار الدفع** + sandbox activate; email/push later
- ✅ Expiry: unpaid intents auto-`expired` (default 48h via `expireStalePurchases`) — no wallet credit
- ✅ All methods write the same ledger shape (`method`, `provider`, `providerRef`, `status`)

#### Ops / compliance checklist (before go-live)

- [ ] Merchant KYC with chosen PSP(s); FRA/CBE-licensed facilitators only
- [ ] PCI scope minimized (hosted / iframe / redirect — no PAN on our servers)
- [ ] Webhook signature verification + replay protection + idempotency keys
- [ ] Settlement currency/schedule documented in Admin (T+N)
- [ ] Refund path per method (InstaPay/Fawry rules differ from cards)
- [ ] Arabic + English failure messages (insufficient funds, expired ref, 3DS fail)

