## 3. Firestore contract (web owns most of these writes)

Collections (names finalizable at implement time; domains are fixed):

| Domain | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `users` / `orgs` | Profile, roles, preferences, `planTier` (`free`/`trial`/`paid`/`partner`) |
| `packages` | Sellable SKUs: price, tokens, period, entitlements |
| `subscriptions` | Active/past package attachment per user |
| `wallets` | Shared balance / remaining tokens (one per account) |
| `payments` / ledger | `provider`, `providerRef`, `method` (`card`/`meeza`/`instapay`/`wallet_*`/`fawry`/…), amount, `currency`, status (`pending`/`paid`/`failed`/`expired`/`refunded`), packageId, userId |
| `usageEvents` | Metering (web + desktop + all devices → **one wallet**) |
| `chats` / `messages` | Conversation continuum |
| `projects` | Web project folders (not git) |
| `libraryItems` | Cloud assets / prompts / bookmarks |
| `plans` | Portable Plan Mode artifact (see §4) |
| `schedules` | Optional Phase 1.5 |
| `devices` / `sessions` | Multi-device awareness (unlimited count; audit only) |

**Security rules:** own-data for users; elevated for admin; payment writes only via trusted Cloud Functions / Admin SDK.  
**Forbidden in Firestore:** workspace source, `.git`, deep index payloads.

