## 4. Plan artifact (must stay aligned with desktop)

Web and desktop must share one Plan shape (see `01-وضع-التخطيط-Plan-Mode.mdc` §3). Conceptual:

```text
Plan {
  id, title, goal,
  status: draft|approved|running|completed|failed|cancelled
  createdAt, updatedAt, chatId?, projectId?
  assumptions[], risks[]
  steps: [{ id, content, status, optional?, hints?, acceptance? }]
  execution?: { startedAt, finishedAt, lastError?, deviceId? }
}
```

Web responsibilities:
- ✅ Create/edit draft plans in UI (true edit / reorder — not prose-only)
- ✅ Approve → `status: approved` in Firestore
- 🟨 Show live statuses while desktop Execute updates the same doc (embed chip; desktop pulls plan on open)
- [ ] Never embed private file contents in `hints` — paths/symbols/names only if needed

Desktop responsibilities (VigilAIAgent — not this repo’s web code):
- Read approved plan → **Execute** with local tools
- Write step statuses + execution fields back to Firestore

